//RS /// c109 Phase 7: parse `src` and return whether the named method on `type_name`
//RS /// (a struct or enum inherent method) is covered by the method gate. Looks up
//RS /// the method in the type's `methods` list. As with `covers`, the
//RS /// sema-dependent facts a method body needs (`recv_type` on inner method calls)
//RS /// are not filled by `build_cx` alone, so the gate paths that consult them are
//RS /// proven by the TIR feature integration targets + the byte-parity check;
//RS /// here we exercise the sema-independent structural gating (self receiver,
//RS /// static shape, param/return types, the `self`-assignment exclusion).
//RS fn covers_method(src: &str, type_name: &str, method: &str) -> bool {
//RS     // Compiler worker required; see `covers`.
